{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G2QXfvrktnXfcKT31GpTMK","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Audiobook Agent - Operational Guide\n     2→\n     3→This guide provides operational commands and codebase navigation for the autonomous improvement loop.\n     4→\n     5→## Running the Analysis Pipeline\n     6→\n     7→### Basic Commands\n     8→\n     9→```bash\n    10→# Full analysis on a text file with HTML output (use --rich-progress for live updates)\n    11→venv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt --html output/gatsby/report.html --output output/gatsby/analysis.json --rich-progress\n    12→\n    13→# With specific models per agent\n    14→venv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt \\\n    15→    --structure-model qwen2.5:14b \\\n    16→    --character-model qwen2.5:32b \\\n    17→    --summary-model qwen2.5:32b \\\n    18→    --pronunciation-model qwen2.5:14b \\\n    19→    --html output/gatsby/report.html \\\n    20→    --rich-progress\n    21→\n    22→# Set default model for all agents\n    23→venv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt --llm-model qwen2.5:32b --html output/gatsby/report.html --rich-progress\n    24→\n    25→# Adjust minimum character mentions threshold\n    26→venv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt --min-mentions 3 --html output/gatsby/report.html --rich-progress\n    27→```\n    28→\n    29→### CLI Options\n    30→\n    31→| Option | Description | Default |\n    32→|--------|-------------|---------|\n    33→| `--output FILE` | JSON output path | `{input_stem}.analysis.json` |\n    34→| `--html FILE` | HTML report path | None |\n    35→| `--tui` | Open interactive TUI after analysis | False |\n    36→| `--wpm N` | Words per minute for duration estimates | 150 |\n    37→| `--min-mentions N` | Minimum character mentions to include | 2 |\n    38→| `--llm-model MODEL` | Default model for all agents | System default |\n    39→| `--structure-model MODEL` | Model for chapter detection | Default |\n    40→| `--character-model MODEL` | Model for character extraction | Default |\n    41→| `--summary-model MODEL` | Model for chapter summaries | Default |\n    42→| `--pronunciation-model MODEL` | Model for pronunciation flags | Default |\n    43→| `--rich-progress` | Show live-updating progress display | False |\n    44→\n    45→## Output Locations\n    46→\n    47→```\n    48→output/\n    49→└── {book_name}/\n    50→    ├── report.html          # HTML report for narrator prep\n    51→    └── analysis.json        # Full JSON analysis data\n    52→```\n    53→\n    54→## Test Texts\n    55→\n    56→Available in `Test_Texts/`:\n    57→- `gatsby.txt` - The Great Gatsby (306 KB)\n    58→- `Frankenstein_ebook.txt` - Frankenstein (421 KB)\n    59→- `East of Eden - East Of Eden.pdf` - East of Eden (1.6 MB)\n    60→- `I_Have_No_Mouth_And_I_Must_Scream.pdf` - Ellison short story (325 KB)\n    61→- `One Hundred Years of Solitude - One_Hundred_Years_of_Solitude.pdf` - Marquez (1.5 MB)\n    62→- `See the Light V-15 11-11-25.docx` - Test document (1.2 MB)\n    63→\n    64→## Key Source Files\n    65→\n    66→### Agent System\n    67→| File | Purpose |\n    68→|------|---------|\n    69→| `src/agents/base.py` | Abstract Agent class with verify/refine methods |\n    70→| `src/agents/structure.py` | StructureAgent - chapter detection |\n    71→| `src/agents/characters.py` | CharacterAgent - character extraction & aliases |\n    72→| `src/agents/summaries.py` | SummaryAgent - chapter summaries |\n    73→| `src/agents/pronunciation.py` | PronunciationAgent - pronunciation flags |\n    74→| `src/agents/config.py` | OrchestratorConfig, per-agent model settings |\n    75→| `src/agents/validation.py` | Upstream validation types |\n    76→\n    77→### Pipeline\n    78→| File | Purpose |\n    79→|------|---------|\n    80→| `src/analyzer.py` | Main orchestrator - runs all agents |\n    81→| `src/pipeline/character_extraction/` | Character NER and extraction |\n    82→| `src/pipeline/character_profiling/` | Character profile generation |\n    83→| `src/pipeline/llm.py` | Unified LLM client (Ollama/OpenAI/Anthropic) |\n    84→| `src/pipeline/metrics.py` | Profiling and metrics |\n    85→\n    86→### Entry Points\n    87→| File | Purpose |\n    88→|------|---------|\n    89→| `src/cli.py` | CLI entry point (`audiobook-prep`) |\n    90→| `src/gui/desktop.py` | Tkinter GUI |\n    91→| `src/gui/tui.py` | Textual-based terminal UI |\n    92→\n    93→### Data Models\n    94→| File | Purpose |\n    95→|------|---------|\n    96→| `src/models.py` | Core Pydantic models (AnalysisResult, Character, etc.) |\n    97→| `src/pipeline/character_extraction/models.py` | Character extraction models |\n    98→| `src/pipeline/character_profiling/models.py` | Character profiling models |\n    99→\n   100→## Configuration\n   101→\n   102→### Agent Model Recommendations\n   103→\n   104→From `src/agents/config.py`:\n   105→\n   106→```python\n   107→RECOMMENDED_AGENT_MODELS = {\n   108→    \"structure\": [\"qwen2.5:14b\", \"qwen2.5:7b\", \"llama3.2\"],\n   109→    \"characters\": [\"qwen2.5:32b\", \"qwen2.5:72b\", \"llama3.1:70b\"],\n   110→    \"summaries\": [\"qwen2.5:32b\", \"qwen2.5:72b\", \"llama3.1:70b\"],\n   111→    \"pronunciation\": [\"qwen2.5:14b\", \"qwen2.5:32b\", \"llama3.2\"],\n   112→}\n   113→```\n   114→\n   115→### Verification Levels\n   116→\n   117→Agents support three verification levels:\n   118→- `STRUCTURAL` - Fast heuristic checks, no LLM\n   119→- `SELF_CHECK` - Local LLM validation, book-agnostic\n   120→- `ORACLE` - Claude-assisted (used by this improvement loop)\n   121→\n   122→## Common Issues & Fixes\n   123→\n   124→### Ollama Connection\n   125→```bash\n   126→# Ensure Ollama is running\n   127→ollama serve\n   128→\n   129→# Check available models\n   130→ollama list\n   131→\n   132→# Pull a model if needed\n   133→ollama pull qwen2.5:32b\n   134→```\n   135→\n   136→### Out of Memory\n   137→- Reduce model size: Use 14b instead of 32b\n   138→- Process shorter texts first\n   139→- Check GPU memory: `nvidia-smi`\n   140→\n   141→### Slow Analysis\n   142→- Full analysis of a novel can take 10-60 minutes\n   143→- Use smaller models for faster iteration during development\n   144→- Check `output/{book}/pipeline.log` for progress\n   145→\n   146→## Testing\n   147→\n   148→```bash\n   149→# Run all tests\n   150→pytest tests/ -v\n   151→\n   152→# Run specific agent tests\n   153→pytest tests/test_character_agent.py -v\n   154→pytest tests/test_structure_agent.py -v\n   155→pytest tests/test_summary_agent.py -v\n   156→pytest tests/test_pronunciation_agent.py -v\n   157→\n   158→# Run alias/merging tests\n   159→pytest tests/test_alias_merging.py -v\n   160→pytest tests/test_coreference.py -v\n   161→\n   162→# Run with coverage\n   163→pytest tests/ --cov=src --cov-report=html\n   164→```\n   165→\n   166→## Loop-Specific Files\n   167→\n   168→| File | Purpose |\n   169→|------|---------|\n   170→| `oracle-loop.sh` | Bash orchestrator for the improvement loop |\n   171→| `PROMPT_analyze.md` | Phase 1 instructions |\n   172→| `PROMPT_evaluate.md` | Phase 2 oracle evaluation instructions |\n   173→| `PROMPT_fix.md` | Phase 3 fix instructions |\n   174→| `manifest.json` | Test text tracking |\n   175→| `EVALUATION_STATE.md` | Current state and issues |\n   176→| `spec/output_quality.md` | Quality evaluation rubric |\n   177→| `logs/` | Iteration logs |\n   178→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17013589-e5ae-4167-b794-171149c21b77","uuid":"0348c3e7-183b-493f-9cfd-c8bb811ba5a4","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/AGENTS.md","content":"# Audiobook Agent - Operational Guide\n\nThis guide provides operational commands and codebase navigation for the autonomous improvement loop.\n\n## Running the Analysis Pipeline\n\n### Basic Commands\n\n```bash\n# Full analysis on a text file with HTML output (use --rich-progress for live updates)\nvenv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt --html output/gatsby/report.html --output output/gatsby/analysis.json --rich-progress\n\n# With specific models per agent\nvenv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt \\\n    --structure-model qwen2.5:14b \\\n    --character-model qwen2.5:32b \\\n    --summary-model qwen2.5:32b \\\n    --pronunciation-model qwen2.5:14b \\\n    --html output/gatsby/report.html \\\n    --rich-progress\n\n# Set default model for all agents\nvenv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt --llm-model qwen2.5:32b --html output/gatsby/report.html --rich-progress\n\n# Adjust minimum character mentions threshold\nvenv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt --min-mentions 3 --html output/gatsby/report.html --rich-progress\n```\n\n### CLI Options\n\n| Option | Description | Default |\n|--------|-------------|---------|\n| `--output FILE` | JSON output path | `{input_stem}.analysis.json` |\n| `--html FILE` | HTML report path | None |\n| `--tui` | Open interactive TUI after analysis | False |\n| `--wpm N` | Words per minute for duration estimates | 150 |\n| `--min-mentions N` | Minimum character mentions to include | 2 |\n| `--llm-model MODEL` | Default model for all agents | System default |\n| `--structure-model MODEL` | Model for chapter detection | Default |\n| `--character-model MODEL` | Model for character extraction | Default |\n| `--summary-model MODEL` | Model for chapter summaries | Default |\n| `--pronunciation-model MODEL` | Model for pronunciation flags | Default |\n| `--rich-progress` | Show live-updating progress display | False |\n\n## Output Locations\n\n```\noutput/\n└── {book_name}/\n    ├── report.html          # HTML report for narrator prep\n    └── analysis.json        # Full JSON analysis data\n```\n\n## Test Texts\n\nAvailable in `Test_Texts/`:\n- `gatsby.txt` - The Great Gatsby (306 KB)\n- `Frankenstein_ebook.txt` - Frankenstein (421 KB)\n- `East of Eden - East Of Eden.pdf` - East of Eden (1.6 MB)\n- `I_Have_No_Mouth_And_I_Must_Scream.pdf` - Ellison short story (325 KB)\n- `One Hundred Years of Solitude - One_Hundred_Years_of_Solitude.pdf` - Marquez (1.5 MB)\n- `See the Light V-15 11-11-25.docx` - Test document (1.2 MB)\n\n## Key Source Files\n\n### Agent System\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `src/agents/base.py` | Abstract Agent class with verify/refine methods |\n| `src/agents/structure.py` | StructureAgent - chapter detection |\n| `src/agents/characters.py` | CharacterAgent - character extraction & aliases |\n| `src/agents/summaries.py` | SummaryAgent - chapter summaries |\n| `src/agents/pronunciation.py` | PronunciationAgent - pronunciation flags |\n| `src/agents/config.py` | OrchestratorConfig, per-agent model settings |\n| `src/agents/validation.py` | Upstream validation types |\n\n### Pipeline\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `src/analyzer.py` | Main orchestrator - runs all agents |\n| `src/pipeline/character_extraction/` | Character NER and extraction |\n| `src/pipeline/character_profiling/` | Character profile generation |\n| `src/pipeline/llm.py` | Unified LLM client (Ollama/OpenAI/Anthropic) |\n| `src/pipeline/metrics.py` | Profiling and metrics |\n\n### Entry Points\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `src/cli.py` | CLI entry point (`audiobook-prep`) |\n| `src/gui/desktop.py` | Tkinter GUI |\n| `src/gui/tui.py` | Textual-based terminal UI |\n\n### Data Models\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `src/models.py` | Core Pydantic models (AnalysisResult, Character, etc.) |\n| `src/pipeline/character_extraction/models.py` | Character extraction models |\n| `src/pipeline/character_profiling/models.py` | Character profiling models |\n\n## Configuration\n\n### Agent Model Recommendations\n\nFrom `src/agents/config.py`:\n\n```python\nRECOMMENDED_AGENT_MODELS = {\n    \"structure\": [\"qwen2.5:14b\", \"qwen2.5:7b\", \"llama3.2\"],\n    \"characters\": [\"qwen2.5:32b\", \"qwen2.5:72b\", \"llama3.1:70b\"],\n    \"summaries\": [\"qwen2.5:32b\", \"qwen2.5:72b\", \"llama3.1:70b\"],\n    \"pronunciation\": [\"qwen2.5:14b\", \"qwen2.5:32b\", \"llama3.2\"],\n}\n```\n\n### Verification Levels\n\nAgents support three verification levels:\n- `STRUCTURAL` - Fast heuristic checks, no LLM\n- `SELF_CHECK` - Local LLM validation, book-agnostic\n- `ORACLE` - Claude-assisted (used by this improvement loop)\n\n## Common Issues & Fixes\n\n### Ollama Connection\n```bash\n# Ensure Ollama is running\nollama serve\n\n# Check available models\nollama list\n\n# Pull a model if needed\nollama pull qwen2.5:32b\n```\n\n### Out of Memory\n- Reduce model size: Use 14b instead of 32b\n- Process shorter texts first\n- Check GPU memory: `nvidia-smi`\n\n### Slow Analysis\n- Full analysis of a novel can take 10-60 minutes\n- Use smaller models for faster iteration during development\n- Check `output/{book}/pipeline.log` for progress\n\n## Testing\n\n```bash\n# Run all tests\npytest tests/ -v\n\n# Run specific agent tests\npytest tests/test_character_agent.py -v\npytest tests/test_structure_agent.py -v\npytest tests/test_summary_agent.py -v\npytest tests/test_pronunciation_agent.py -v\n\n# Run alias/merging tests\npytest tests/test_alias_merging.py -v\npytest tests/test_coreference.py -v\n\n# Run with coverage\npytest tests/ --cov=src --cov-report=html\n```\n\n## Loop-Specific Files\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `oracle-loop.sh` | Bash orchestrator for the improvement loop |\n| `PROMPT_analyze.md` | Phase 1 instructions |\n| `PROMPT_evaluate.md` | Phase 2 oracle evaluation instructions |\n| `PROMPT_fix.md` | Phase 3 fix instructions |\n| `manifest.json` | Test text tracking |\n| `EVALUATION_STATE.md` | Current state and issues |\n| `spec/output_quality.md` | Quality evaluation rubric |\n| `logs/` | Iteration logs |\n","numLines":178,"startLine":1,"totalLines":178}}}
